.TH HALCYON-TUI 1 "November 2026" "halcyon 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
halcyon-tui \\- terminal front end for the Halcyon console
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B halcyon-tui
[\\fB\\-\\-url\\fR \\fIURL\\fR] [\\fB\\-\\-once\\fR] [\\fB\\-\\-send\\fR \\fITEXT\\fR]
[\\fB\\-\\-link\\fR \\fITEXT\\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B halcyon-tui
draws the station console in a terminal for machines that have no browser: a
headless box or an SSH session.  It is a client of the loopback JSON API served
by
.BR halcyon (1),
not a second modem, so the console has to be running first:
.PP
.RS 4
python3 -m halcyon.ui --port 8730
.RE
.PP
Status rows show the radio, the modem host, CAT and TCI, the current profile and
speed level.  The scope pane shows the receiver spectrum (or the waterfall of
the last burst) and the transcript records traffic and errors.  Messages, link
tests and radio, host and CAT commands go through the console, so they behave as
they do in the browser page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \\-\\-url " " \\fIURL\\fR
Console to attach to.  Defaults to \\fIhttp://127.0.0.1:8730\\fR.
.TP
.B \\-\\-once
Draw one frame, print it and exit.  A piped standard output does the same.
.TP
.BR \\-\\-send " " \\fITEXT\\fR
Send a message through the simulated channel and show what the console
decoded.  Implies \\fB\\-\\-once\\fR.
.TP
.BR \\-\\-link " " \\fITEXT\\fR
Run the console's adaptive link test.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B m
Compose and send a message.
.TP
.B p
Next profile; \\fB+\\fR and \\fB\\-\\fR move one speed level.
.TP
.B l
Run an ARQ transfer.
.TP
.B s
Start or stop the modem host.
.TP
.B d
Discover and connect the first Hermes Lite 2; \\fBx\\fR disconnects it.
.TP
.B r
Refresh the console state.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HALCYON_URL
Console URL used when \\fB\\-\\-url\\fR is absent.
.TP
.B HALCYON_MYCALL
Call sign reported when the terminal starts the modem host.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR halcyon (1),
.BR halcyon-gui (1)
.SH AUTHOR
The Halcyon authors.
